windows: daemon over a protected named pipe, protected processes, no loopback servers

Clauseo's patch to vercel-labs/agent-browser v0.41.1, applied after 0001. Windows code paths
only; macOS and Linux behave as upstream (plus 0001).

- The daemon listens on \\.\pipe\clauseo-ab-<128-bit random hex> instead of loopback TCP. The id
  is written to <session>.pipe in the socket directory (never a command-line argument). The first
  instance is created with FILE_FLAG_FIRST_PIPE_INSTANCE; every instance has a protected DACL for
  the user and SYSTEM and rejects remote clients. After a client connects the daemon reads its
  process token (GetNamedPipeClientProcessId, OpenProcessToken, IsTokenRestricted) and
  disconnects a restricted client, or any it cannot check, before writing a byte. The client
  connects at SECURITY_IDENTIFICATION and refuses a pipe whose GetNamedPipeServerProcessId is not
  the pid in <session>.pid.
- Every agent-browser process applies
  D:P(A;;0x1FFFFF;;;SY)(A;;0x101000;;;<user SID>)(A;;0x101000;;;OW) to itself first thing in
  main, and starts the daemon (from the CLI) and the CLI (from the MCP server) with the same
  descriptor in CreateProcessW's lpProcessAttributes, inheriting only their stdio handles.
- Streaming is always off on Windows (0001's switch is forced on); the dashboard and the inspect
  proxy refuse to start on Windows.

